Tracked placeholder for episodes/active/ — the ordinary rhyme-search set.

Git does not track empty directories, so without a tracked file here this directory
would vanish at commit and the layout the store depends on would exist only on the
machine that created it. Gate g1 of issue #301 hit exactly that with episodes/ itself.

Why this file is NOT a README.md: inside active/ and retired/ every Markdown file IS an
episode — membership is the directory, not a parsed field — so the store classifies a
file by its own id grammar (`<kebab-case-run>-NNN.md`, `episode_id_for()` in
scripts/apply_episode_delta.py). A `README.md` here is not a well-formed episode
filename and is refused as malformed; the first attempt at this layout shipped one and
minted the phantom episode id `README` in both directories, which made the whole store
unreadable. A placeholder that is not a `.md` file cannot be mistaken for a record.

What lives here, how retirement moves a file out of it, and why: ../README.md and
docs/EPISODE_STORE.md §7. Nothing here is hand-edited —
scripts/apply_episode_delta.py is the only write path.
